{"id":"608d9956db5b7013","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-thm-lebesgue-diff.md","title":"Lebesgue Differentiation","display":"thm-lebesgue-diff — Lebesgue Differentiation","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-lebesgue-diff","aliases":["58-thm-lebesgue-diff"],"display":"thm-lebesgue-diff — Lebesgue Differentiation","depends_on":["[[58-df-function]]","[[58-df-measure]]","[[58-df-measurable-function]]","[[58-df-integral]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-lebesgue-diff"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-lebesgue-diff</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-lebesgue-diff — Lebesgue Differentiation"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"58-df-measure\">58-df-measure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"bbbec05fde1d3b01\" href=\"?note=bbbec05fde1d3b01\" title=\"58-df-measurable-function\">58-df-measurable-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"4884f45058a56aac\" href=\"?note=4884f45058a56aac\" title=\"58-df-integral\">58-df-integral</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Explicit relation signatures used below: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}\">\\(\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measure}_S\\subseteq V^{3}\">\\(\\mathrm{Measure}_S\\subseteq V^{3}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\\subseteq V^{5}\">\\(\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\\subseteq V^{5}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f,\\lambda_n,\\mathcal L_n\\in V\">\\(f,\\lambda_n,\\mathcal L_n\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda_n\">\\(\\lambda_n\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L_n\">\\(\\mathcal L_n\\)</span> are the standard <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>-dimensional Lebesgue measure and its completed sigma-algebra on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R^n\">\\(\\mathbb R^n\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B_r(x)=\\{y\\in\\mathbb R^n:\\|y-x\\|&lt;r\\}\">\\(B_r(x)=\\{y\\in\\mathbb R^n:\\|y-x\\|&lt;r\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B(\\mathbb C)\">\\(\\mathcal B(\\mathbb C)\\)</span> is the Borel sigma-algebra on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb C\">\\(\\mathbb C\\)</span></li>\n<li>Local integrability is expanded below as measurability plus finite integral on every centered finite-radius ball</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}lebesgue\\text{-}diff}\\vdash{}&amp;\nn\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\n\\land\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\lambda_n,\\mathbb R^n,\\mathcal L_n)\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(f,\\mathbb R^n,\\mathbb C)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\n\\bigl(f;(\\mathbb R^n,\\mathcal L_n),(\\mathbb C,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb C))\\bigr)\n\\land\\forall R\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\int_{B_R(0)}|f(y)|\\,d\\lambda_n(y)&lt;\\infty\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\lambda_n\\!\\left(\n\\left\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^n:\n\\lim_{r\\downarrow0}\\frac{1}{\\lambda_n(B_r(x))}\n\\int_{B_r(x)}|f(y)-f(x)|\\,d\\lambda_n(y)\\neq0\n\\right\\}\\right)=0.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}lebesgue\\text{-}diff}\\vdash{}&amp;\nn\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\n\\land\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\lambda_n,\\mathbb R^n,\\mathcal L_n)\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(f,\\mathbb R^n,\\mathbb C)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\n\\bigl(f;(\\mathbb R^n,\\mathcal L_n),(\\mathbb C,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb C))\\bigr)\n\\land\\forall R\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\int_{B_R(0)}|f(y)|\\,d\\lambda_n(y)&lt;\\infty\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\lambda_n\\!\\left(\n\\left\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^n:\n\\lim_{r\\downarrow0}\\frac{1}{\\lambda_n(B_r(x))}\n\\int_{B_r(x)}|f(y)-f(x)|\\,d\\lambda_n(y)\\neq0\n\\right\\}\\right)=0.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Lebesgue differentiation theorem.</li>\n<li>The stronger standard form—mean oscillation about <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f(x)\">\\(f(x)\\)</span> tends to zero—is stated with its dimension and reference measure explicit.  “Almost everywhere” is no longer an undeclared quantifier: the exceptional set is required to have <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda_n\">\\(\\lambda_n\\)</span>-measure zero.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-measure","status":"resolved","id":"ca832ed6bc22f728","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-measure]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-measurable-function","status":"resolved","id":"bbbec05fde1d3b01","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-measurable-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-integral","status":"resolved","id":"4884f45058a56aac","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-integral]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Measure}_S\\subseteq V^{3}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\\subseteq V^{5}","display":false},{"tex":"n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}","display":false},{"tex":"f,\\lambda_n,\\mathcal L_n\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\lambda_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal L_n","display":false},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R^n","display":false},{"tex":"B_r(x)=\\{y\\in\\mathbb R^n:\\|y-x\\|<r\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal B(\\mathbb C)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb C","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}lebesgue\\text{-}diff}\\vdash{}&\nn\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\n\\land\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\lambda_n,\\mathbb R^n,\\mathcal L_n)\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(f,\\mathbb R^n,\\mathbb C)\\\\\n&\\land\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\n\\bigl(f;(\\mathbb R^n,\\mathcal L_n),(\\mathbb C,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb C))\\bigr)\n\\land\\forall R\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\n\\int_{B_R(0)}|f(y)|\\,d\\lambda_n(y)<\\infty\\\\\n&\\to\\lambda_n\\!\\left(\n\\left\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^n:\n\\lim_{r\\downarrow0}\\frac{1}{\\lambda_n(B_r(x))}\n\\int_{B_r(x)}|f(y)-f(x)|\\,d\\lambda_n(y)\\neq0\n\\right\\}\\right)=0.\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"f(x)","display":false},{"tex":"\\lambda_n","display":false}],"bytes":1862,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4276","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-thm-lebesgue-diff.md|58-thm-lebesgue-diff]]（batch19）"}],"outgoing":["36d7463d215be751","ca832ed6bc22f728","bbbec05fde1d3b01","4884f45058a56aac"]}